---
number: 254
title: With a Sorrow For Sin
author: R. Saillens
composer: E. G. Taylor
sp_category: "18"
topic: Repentance and Acceptance
notes: "AUTO: chorus detected heuristically — verify"
---

[verse 1]
With a sorrow for sin must repentance begin,
Then salvation of course will draw nigh;
But till washed in the blood of the crucified Lord,
You will never be ready to die.

[chorus]
Look, Look, look and live!
There is life for a look at the crucified One,
There is life at this moment for thee.

[verse 2]
We’ve His word and His oath, and His blood seals them both
And we’re sure the Almighty can’t lie
If you do not delay, but repent while you may,
He will soon make you ready to die.

[chorus]
Look, Look, look and live!
There is life for a look at the crucified One,
There is life at this moment for thee.

[verse 3]
And that you may succeed, come along with all speed
To a Saviour who will not deny;
So kneel down at His feet, at the blest mercy seat,
And He’ll soon make you ready to die.

[chorus]
Look, Look, look and live!
There is life for a look at the crucified One,
There is life at this moment for thee.
